<section class="part">
<h2 class="sec">Part 1 · The audit</h2>
<p class="body">Document what you actually consumed over the past week, not what you wish you had consumed. Be specific.</p>
<p class="body"><b>For each source or platform you regularly get information from:</b></p>
<ul class="qlist">
<li>What is it? Name, platform, type.</li>
<li>How often do you check it? Daily, a few times a week, when bored.</li>
<li>What kind of information does it give you? News, opinions, tutorials, entertainment, other people's takes.</li>
<li>Did you choose it deliberately, or did it become a habit?</li>
</ul>
<div class="rbox">
<label class="qt" for="bx-b1"><b>My sources.</b> One source per line, with the four answers.</label>
<textarea class="box" id="bx-b1" data-key="b1"></textarea>
</div>
<p class="body"><b>Then answer:</b></p>
<ul class="qlist">
<li>What patterns do you notice? Are most of your sources the same type, the same platform, the same perspective?</li>
<li>What is missing? Which topics, viewpoints or kinds of source are absent?</li>
<li>What do these sources help you understand or do? What other purposes do they serve, such as connection, enjoyment, or keeping up with events?</li>
</ul>
<div class="rbox">
<label class="qt" for="bx-b2"><b>What I notice.</b> The patterns, what is missing, and what purposes my sources serve.</label>
<textarea class="box" id="bx-b2" data-key="b2"></textarea>
</div>
</section>

<section class="part">
<h2 class="sec">Part 2 · One change, for my Sprint 3 goal</h2>
<p class="body">Choose one change to your information diet that would help your Sprint 3 goal: add, replace, reduce, or use a source differently. A source can be a person, program, publication, community, or feed. Explain what you will change, why it fits your goal, how often you will use the source between now and 30 November, and how the change will affect the time you spend.</p>
<div class="rbox">
<label class="qt" for="bx-b3"><b>My one change.</b> The change, why it fits my goal, how often, and how it affects my time.</label>
<textarea class="box" id="bx-b3" data-key="b3"></textarea>
</div>
</section>

<h2 class="sec">Submit</h2>
<p class="body">Press <b>Copy my answers</b> and paste the text into the Canvas text box. The audit is complete when the list is honest; a short honest list is a finished audit.</p>
<div class="copywrap">
<button type="button" class="btn primary" id="copy-btn">Copy my answers</button>
<div class="status" id="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
<label class="qt" for="summary-out" style="margin-top:10px">The text that gets copied</label>
<textarea class="sumout" id="summary-out" readonly></textarea>
</div>
<p class="body" style="margin-top:14px">Once you have done this, you know where your attention goes and you have chosen how to use it for the rest of the sprint. Questions go to Prof. Sathya or the TA.</p>
<p class="storenote">This browser is blocking local storage, so what you type in the boxes will not survive a reload. Press Copy my answers before you leave the page, and keep the text in a document of your own.</p>

